  "tf_bot_infos": {
  "tl": "BotInfo",
  "_folded_scalar_note": "`description` is a COLUMN here, not a child. `BotInfo` declares `description:flags.1?string` (schema/sources/TL_telegram_v227.tl:697) \u2014 a plain `string` scalar, so the wire nests nothing there. `2026_10_11_000100_fold_bot_infos_description_onto_the_bot_info_fact.php` dropped the fabricated `tf_bot_infos_description` table and moved the value up here, and re-parented `tf_bot_infos_description_{photo,document}` onto `tf_bot_infos`, which is where `description_photo:flags.4?Photo` and `description_document:flags.5?Document` actually live \u2014 the catalog declared those two as children of `tf_bot_infos` all along, and the shipped FK pointed at the fabricated table only because `MirrorRelationPlan::reflect()` picks a child parent by LONGEST name prefix. The `description` child entry stayed listed here until this edit, which left `MirrorFactWriter` inserting into a table the dial no longer creates: an ingest-time break, not a cosmetic one.",
  "ctors": [
   "botInfo"
  ],
